Z||000000||Philphine||06-26-2001||11:10 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.corvetteforum.cc/ubb/Forum3/HTML/029608.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.corvetteforum.cc/ubb/Forum3/HTML/029608.html</A> <P>the '74 described in this thread about matches mine. i have the low hp 350 (i think. a few people have looked at it and weren't sure if it was the original engine). so i'm figuring my '87 fiero has somewhere bettween a 6-800lb. weight advantage (depending on how you split hairs). i've wanted the effort of a swap to be worth it and now i'm feeling better about a 4.5-9 swap.<P>take into consideration i wasn't around high perf. cars coming up so even though about 200hp isn't much it's always felt pretty strong to me. drop a 1/4 ton of weight and i ought to be happier still. plus if the choptop project gets anywhere maybe i can go for something more next go round.<P>so the decision is made. the '87 will get a pre-northstar caddy engine.<P>i think. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (project. or at least an interesting collection of parts)||||reg||1
